   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2021 directing the urban development\ncorporation to conduct a study regarding the assistance needed to encourage\nwomen and minorities to pursue technology careers in science, technology,\nengineering and mathematics (STEM), as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS. 531-B and A. 530-B, in relation to the frequency of updates to the report\non such study",
    "basePrintNo": "S7842",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7842-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap of 2021 (as proposed in S.531-B & A.530-B)",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7842\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2021 directing the urban devel-\nopment corporation to conduct a study regarding the assistance needed to\nencourage women and minorities to pursue technology careers in science,\ntechnology, engineering and mathematics (STEM), as proposed in legisla-\ntive bills numbers S. 531-B and A. 530-B, in relation to the frequency\nof updates to the report on such study\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of 1.2021,\nc.757.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter to require the report due\nevery two years, rather than annually.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 119 of 2021, the Executive supports a modifi-\ncation that provides that the UDC provide a report on this critical\ntopic every two years.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 757 of the Laws of 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
